BS_:

BU_: BCM BCW CAMERA CLU DATC EMS ESC IBOX LCA LVR PGS SCC SMK SNV TCU TPMS Vector__XXX XXX _4WD

CM_ "imported_from_opendbc.dbc";
CM_ "source: /home/trh/Packages/opendbc";
CM_ "logs: /home/trh/Packages/Ioniq5_CAN/CAN_logs";
CM_ "only messages validated against the logs are defined below";
CM_ "every BO_/SG_/VAL_/SG_MUL_VAL_ line is copied verbatim from the opendbc source file named in its comment";
CM_ "Not imported, although the frame id matches the logs:";
CM_ "0x316  opendbc EMS11/EMS1 layout is wrong here: bytes 3-7 are constant, byte 2 is an alive counter, bytes 0-1 a checksum. The 'N = 304 rpm' reading is the counter.";
CM_ "0x251  opendbc MDPS12 layout is wrong here: CF_Mdps_Chksum2 (byte 3) is always 0x00 and bytes 4-7 are always 0; only the byte-2 counter lines up (+2 per frame).";
CM_ "0x180  checksum-proven (173/173) but opendbc has no correct 8-byte definition: the 8-byte entry is AMP_HU_PE_01 (audio amp) and CAM_0x180 is declared 32 bytes.";
CM_ "0x06F, 0x385  checksum-proven but no opendbc message definition exists.";
CM_ "Remaining frame-id matches are from the 2015-era platform files and were never payload-verified; importing them would add ~70 unverified messages. See dbc_log_overlap_report.txt section 3 for the full list.";

CM_ "0x185 CAM_0x185 from opendbc/dbc/hyundai_canfd_generated.dbc: T1 checksum-proven: 173/173 frames match hkg_can_fd_checksum()";
BO_ 389 CAM_0x185: 8 CAMERA
 SG_ CHECKSUM : 0|16@1+ (1,0) [0|65535] "" XXX
 SG_ COUNTER : 16|8@1+ (1,0) [0|255] "" XXX

